assertion  XSH.iswprint.001
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswprint() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class print as the locale definition lists it: the letters,
           the digits, the punctuation and the space.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswprint.002
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswprint() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the control characters.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswprint.003
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswprint(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswprint.004
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each of the 128 characters, iswprint() is non-zero exactly when
           iswgraph() is non-zero or the character is the space.
test       t/004-print-is-graph-or-space.c

assertion  XSH.iswprint.005
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswprint.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale, iswprint() is still non-zero for the letters,
           the digits and the space.
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
